\f1\fs22 Sarah woke up, threw up, and was at once both mortally confused and perniciously terrified.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah never got sick, never had a sore throat or a runny nose nor a headache. She doubted she\'92d ever had bad breath. But on this day, some three weeks since Tony had been rounded up by the police or at the behest of the commandants of Public Safety Broadcasting, she suffered all of the aforementioned. And being blankly unaccustomed to such kinds of fragility, Sarah felt her throat excoriated and acid-washed; her nose a clagged high-pressure hose threatening to drown her; her skull a multi-bladed food processor for her brain; her spittle the product of a sewer full of minced bison droppings and ostrich feathers.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The decor of bedroom in the mansion in which the Elvi had house-arrested her (mansion-arrested?) only amplified her agony; the walls were blood-red, the curtains altogether too frilly, and the broadcast screens in the ceiling above the bed, one of which had a crazed bullet hole in it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She called for Nancy the housekeeper, who assisted her out of bed and to the bathroom, its garish decor driving another trio of blender blades between her eyes. She hated gold fittings. The tiled walls that looked like enormous petrified crossword puzzles hurt her eyes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah launched past the toilet, aiming for the circular ceramic cloister of the shower where she hurled indiscriminently.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I\'92ll call the doctor,\'92 soothed Nancy the housekeeper.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'92No,\'92 Sarah said through jaws working to keep her from retching. \'91This will pass.\'92\
\pard\pardeftab360\sl360\slmult1\partightenfactor0

