\f1\fs22 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Since he\'92d disappeared the morning after the Vegas Show, and CEO Piotr Dunhilton declared him Cloudborne Enemy #1, the episode of various goons assisting Tony with his confessions was on constant rotation on CurbTV. Sarah morbidly watched the show ever since the Elvi offered her\'97that is, jailed her in\'97the mansion, \'91
\f3\i for her own good\'92
\f1\i0 . Each time she was unable to look away as she fought back tears and her lip trembled. As bleak and bloody as it was, the show was Sarah\'92s most tangible connection with Tony. Even though she could almost feel every assault upon him, every day she meekly obeyed the remote control button as it persuaded her of the harmless ease of pressing it. With each repeat of the episode, Sarah lost a little of herself as Tony blithely bit back anguish and tongued his teeth, surveying the damage, as he winced and confessed over and over, 
\f3\i I don\'92t know
\f1\i0 .
\f3\i \

\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>He never begged; he never pleaded. He never bargained.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Goon: 
\f3\i  You kidnapped Sarah Jacobson.
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony: 
\f3\i I don\'92t know who that is.\

\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Goon: 
\f3\i Tell us where you\'92re keeping Sarah Jacobson.\

\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony: 
\f3\i I don\'92t know where she is.\

\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>That was the most distressful part. And the sweetest.\
