\f1\fs22 After the first week, it dawned on the habitualised and traumatised Sarah there was more than one episode. She distinguished three for certain, and another three were added to rotation the following week. On average a new episode aired every two days, yet Tony appeared fresh and unbroken on the commencement of each episode. Sarah convinced herself it was an editing technique, where a single session was cut to look like several free-standing encounters. As new episodes continued to appear during the third week, Sarah tested her hypothesis and, with an ever-critical eye, she saw various continuity errors, the most obvious of which, now she saw it, was the condition of Tony\'92s prison overalls, which were becoming consistently more bloody and soiled from episode to episode, even as Tony\'92s face and fingers blushed with renewal.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>If Sarah knew no better, she would say Tony was almost invincible. But she did know better, and conceded Tony\'92s fast-healing powers anyway. Her blood chilled as she contemplated the means by which Tony must have attained such physical advantages.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s hand grabbed the side-table handle, pulled the drawer back and reached inside for an object she implicitly knew would be there. With it, she put a bullet in the 2
