\f1\fs22 An hour later saw Sarah immersed in foundation-cracking music, dancing naked and jumping on the ornate bed. So vigorous and committed was her merriment, she neither noticed nor would have cared about the shards of broadcast screen glass falling in her hair and on the regal bed covers. As she danced, she salved her inferno-grade thirst from a briefcase-sized water bottle.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The next morning, Sarah reflected on the nature of mortality as she pressed her forehead and nose against the grate of the shower drain, and hoped her stomach had done with turning itself inside-out for the day.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dr John arrived with a different Dr Nick. Sarah realised this Dr John was another clone of entirely different \'85 well, nothing, really since he was a clone. He, like the former Dr John, also prescribed Dr Nick\'92s Mix.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I have plenty of that, thank you,\'92 Sarah said while cradling her sore head. \'91Good day.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The next Dr John summoned by Nancy prescribed a peanut butter colonic.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>After Nancy dispatched the latest of the Change of Habit Series, Sarah told her, \'91I want a real doctor.\'92
